# Split olean-cache tarball parts. scripts/lean-olean-cache-seed.sh builds these
# in the repo root even on a dry run, and they are ~90 MB each — above GitHub's
# blob limit. They belong only on the lake-cache/* orphan branches, never on a
# work branch.
lake-oleans.tgz.part*
lake-oleans.tgz

# qou-vbw1 A2 verification aid (resumable I-cache + log); see qbeta_3bp8_a2_sample_point_delta_check.py
.a2_icache.json
.a2_run.log

# Agent scratch state — never repository content. A sandbox accumulates these
# as untracked directories; a `git add -A` then sweeps them into a commit whose
# message describes something else entirely. That is how commit 85ea8e55
# ("Hecke: rank axiom") came to add 46,155 files / 11.4M insertions, including
# 14,688 duplicate beans. None of these is listed in AGENTS.md §Project
# structure. (`uploads/` IS a documented intake pipeline — deliberately absent.)
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash — root-level only, deliberately. A gitignore
# pattern containing no internal slash matches at EVERY depth, so the earlier
# unanchored `_deprecated/` silently captured two documented archives:
# `computations/_deprecated/` (1,449 tracked files: README, witnesses, and
# `script-qa/*.script-qa.json` QA sidecars) and `docs/audits/_deprecated/`
# (66 files). Tracked files were unaffected — ignore rules never untrack — but
# any NEW file under either path would have been dropped by `git add` with no
# error, which is the same silent-loss shape this block exists to prevent.
# Keep the leading slash on every entry here.
/.agents/
/amalgamated_done/
/amalgamated_input/
/_deprecated/
/scratch/

# convention-C regeneration harness runtime lock (SerialLock, O_EXCL). Carries
# an internal slash, so it is already anchored to this file's directory by
# gitignore semantics — consistent with the leading-slash rule above, which
# only needs stating for patterns that have no slash of their own.
.work/*.lock
